Once again someone who incorrectly thought they knew what they were talking
about has posted authoritative-sounding replies to questions without even
acknowledging the fact they were really guessing.  I hate to editorialize,
but I find this extremely ANNOYING!  If you're going to answer a question,
well and good, but at least take the time to make sure you're right.  This
way you avoid getting some hapless newcomer killed (or at least inconvenienced)
and, more importantly, avoid the ire of such folk as myself.  Such obviously
humble folk as myself :) 
	Anyway, for those of you who are wondering what I'm talking about,
it was claimed that
1. Enchant armor scrolls enchant a random piece of armor.  Wrong.  They enchant
 the outermost piece (cloak before armor before Hawaiian shirt, for instance.)
2. Enchanting a +3 piece of armor will dissolve it.  Again wrong.  The odds
 of detroying armor, unless I'm much mistaken, are 1/(the current bonus of
 the armor).  I'm not sure what happens if the armor has a negative bonus, or
 if what I've said is true for +2 armor (but I think it is).
3. That blessed armor reduces the probability that undead will hit you.  Unless
 this is new to 3.1, it isn't true.  (Where do people get this stuff? Do they
 make it up?)  The only use in blessing armor is it takes longer for liches
 and such to curse. (One curse to make it uncursed, and then another to curse.)

OK, end of diatribe.  Thank you and good day.

